5. Experimental Realization and Feasibility

5.1 Phases

Phase I — Physicochemical characterization. CMC, micelle hydrodynamic radius, zeta potential, surface tension, sebum solubilization capacity, pH trajectory, ZN.

Phase II — Barrier interaction. \Delta\text{pH}, \Delta\text{TEWL}, lipid extraction by chromatography, protein denaturation by CD, FTIR, ZN. Explants and in vivo.

Phase III — Differential detersion. R_i for sebum by gravimetry, particulate matter, lipophilic pollutants, targeted pathogens. Selective cleansing benchmarks: oleic acid removal versus squalane sparing, per the BCME paradigm, with sodium surfactin as the specific selectivity booster.

Phase IV — Microbiome dynamics. 16S/metagenomic sequencing, CLR with count-based Bayesian-multiplicative replacement, multi-metric d_{\text{microbe}}, \tau_{\text{rec}} at pre-registered \epsilon, network topology, absolute abundance by qPCR, CFU, PMA-ddPCR.

Phase V — Integrated validation. Pareto front construction over non-dominated candidates from Phases I–IV, using the maximal set under \prec_{\epsilon}. Test H_{\text{local, acute}} and H_{\text{local, cumulative}}. Report the full non-dominated set. Sensitivity analysis across metrics, zero-handling protocols, and \epsilon tolerances.

5.2 Funnel and Feasibility

The staged design implies a pre-registered elimination funnel. Expected survival fractions are:

|\mathcal{U}_{\text{adm}}'| \approx 594
\;\xrightarrow{\text{Tier 1}}\;
\sim 150
\;\xrightarrow{\text{Tier 2}}\;
\sim 60
\;\xrightarrow{\text{Tier 3}}\;
\sim 20
\;\xrightarrow{\text{Tier 4}}\;
\sim 5

The Tier 4 confirmatory arm operates on the order of 5 \times 32 = 160 subjects. Tier 3 screening operates on the order of 60 \times 8 = 480 subject-sessions. The wet-lab program across Phases I–IV, at the screening scale, is bounded and estimable. Cost and timeline are pre-registered alongside the protocol.

