PMA at 2.5–15 µM effectively inhibited PCR amplification of DNA from membrane-compromised cells, reducing 16S rRNA gene copies by 24–44% relative to untreated samples. QMP captured significant shifts in community composition across samples with decreasing proportions of intact cells, whereas RMP failed to detect abundance changes at ASV level.

