Appendix C: Instrument Specifications and Measurement Protocols

C.1 TEWL Measurement

Instrument: Tewameter TM300 (Courage + Khazaka, Cologne, Germany). Open-chamber evaporimeter.

Reproducibility: The TM300 has a reported coefficient of variation (CV) ranging from 0.86% to 17.70%, with mean CV = 6.08% and SD = 3.57% across in vitro measurements. In vivo validation against the TM Hex reports CV = 19% for TM300. For the \epsilon_{\text{TEWL}} tolerance, the upper 95% confidence bound on the relative CV is used, yielding:

\epsilon_{\text{TEWL}} = \frac{1.5}{\overline{\text{TEWL}}_{\text{base}}}

where 1.5 g/m²/h represents the upper bound on instrument reproducibility at typical baseline TEWL values.

Measurement conditions: Measurements performed in a climate-controlled room at 21 ± 1°C and 50 ± 5% relative humidity. Subjects acclimatized for 20 minutes prior to measurement. Probe placed perpendicular to skin surface for 30 seconds until stable reading.

C.2 pH Measurement

Instrument: Glass electrode pH meter calibrated with standard buffers at pH 4.0 and 7.0.

Reproducibility: Glass electrode reproducibility yields \epsilon_{\text{pH}} = 0.2 / \overline{\text{pH}}_{\text{base}}. The relative tolerance is derived from the electrode's documented reproducibility of ±0.02 pH units, scaled to the baseline pH.

C.3 Zein Number Assay

Principle: Zein (corn protein) solubilization by surfactant solutions measured as nitrogen content in the filtrate.

Protocol: 1% (w/w) surfactant solution mixed with zein powder (2 g/40 mL) for 1 hour at room temperature. Filtrate nitrogen determined by Kjeldahl method. Results expressed as mg N per 100 g surfactant solution.

Classification thresholds (Bujak et al.): ZN > 400 mg/100 mL = highly irritating; ZN 200–400 = moderately irritating; ZN < 200 = mildly irritating.

C.4 CMC and Micelle Characterization

CMC: Determined by surface tension titration (Wilhelmy plate method) and conductivity.

Micelle hydrodynamic radius: Dynamic light scattering (DLS) at 25°C.

Zeta potential: Electrophoretic light scattering (Zetasizer).

Micelle diffusion coefficient: Derived from DLS via Stokes–Einstein relation.

C.5 Sebum Removal (Gravimetry)

Protocol: Standardized sebum loading with artificial sebum (composition: triglycerides 40%, wax esters 25%, squalene 15%, fatty acids 15%, cholesterol 5%). Cleansing under controlled conditions (1 mL formulation, 30 s contact, 10 s rinse). Residual sebum extracted with chloroform/methanol (2:1) and gravimetrically quantified.

