Appendix D: Regulatory Framework Details

D.1 EU Regulation 1223/2009 and Amendment 2017/1224

Methylisothiazolinone (MIT) is restricted to a maximum concentration of 0.0015% (15 ppm) in rinse-off cosmetic products, effective 27 January 2018 for new market placements and 27 April 2018 for all products on the market.

Prohibited substances relevant to the surfactant grid include those listed in Annex II of Regulation 1223/2009. The admissible space \mathcal{U}_{\text{adm}}' filters formulations containing any prohibited substance or exceeding restricted-substance limits.

D.2 Regulatory Filter Operationalization

The constraint set \mathcal{R} is applied as:

\mathcal{U}_{\text{adm}}' = \{u \in \mathcal{U}_{\text{adm}} \mid u \text{ satisfies } \mathcal{R}\}

The filter is applied after enumeration of the full Cartesian product but before any experimental testing. The filter reduces the cardinality of \mathcal{U}_{\text{adm}} by removing formulations that are not marketable under EU regulation.

