Appendix E: Compositional Data Analysis Protocol

E.1 Zero Handling: Bayesian-Multiplicative Replacement

The cmultRepl function from the zCompositions R package is used with the following parameters:

· Prior: Dirichlet with geometric mean marginals.
· Replacement: Posterior mean of the zero cell, \hat{\delta}_j.
· Threshold: Detection limit calibrated per sequencing run (default \delta_j = 0.5 counts).

The replacement is applied to counts before closure, preserving the compositional total in expectation.

E.2 CLR Transformation

After replacement, counts are closed to proportions and CLR-transformed:

\text{clr}(x_{ij}) = \log\left(\frac{x_{ij}}{g(\mathbf{x}_i)}\right)

where g(\mathbf{x}_i) is the geometric mean of the composition for sample i.

E.3 Distance Metrics

Metric Primary/Secondary \epsilon default
Aitchison distance Primary 1 SD of baseline
Bray–Curtis dissimilarity Secondary 0.3
UniFrac (weighted, unweighted) Exploratory —

Sensitivity analysis across all metrics is mandated.

E.4 Absolute Abundance Vector

\text{Abund}(t) = \left(\text{qPCR}, \; \text{CFU}, \; \text{PMA-ddPCR}\right)

Absolute abundance is analyzed separately from compositional metrics. PMA treatment at 2.5–15 µM is applied prior to ddPCR.

