Appendix H: Statistical Analysis Plan

H.1 Confirmatory Family

The confirmatory family consists of Tier 4 tests across the non-dominated candidate set from Tier 3 (expected ~20 formulations, of which ~5 pass Tier 4). The family is pre-registered.

H.2 Multiplicity Control

Benjamini–Hochberg procedure at false discovery rate q = 0.05 across the confirmatory family. Applied once at the Tier 4 stage. Tier 3 screening is exempt because it produces no inferential claims.

H.3 Power

For Tier 4: effect size d = 0.8 on at least two primary dimensions, \alpha = 0.05, power = 0.80, 20% dropout yields n \ge 32 subjects per formulation.

H.4 \epsilon-Dominance Test

For u, v \in \mathcal{U}_{\text{adm}}':

u \prec_{\epsilon} v \iff (1 + \epsilon_i)\, \mathcal{D}_{\text{primary},i}(u) \le \mathcal{D}_{\text{primary},i}(v) \quad \forall\, i \in \{1, \dots, 5\}

with strict inequality for at least one i. The \epsilon-Pareto front is the maximal set under \prec_{\epsilon}.

H.5 Non-Inferiority Test

R(u) \ge R(u_{\text{base}}) - \Delta_{\text{NI}}

with \Delta_{\text{NI}} = 10\% of baseline sebum removal. One-sided non-inferiority test at \alpha = 0.025.

H.6 Sensitivity Analyses

Pre-registered sensitivity analyses across:

· Compositional distance metrics (Aitchison, Bray–Curtis, UniFrac).
· Zero-handling protocols (multiplicative replacement, Bayesian-multiplicative replacement).
· \epsilon tolerances (derived values ± 25%).

